1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,478
Last time this was three balls of rock.

2
00:00:03,928 --> 00:00:12,624
Today it is a cave with a hall somebody built in it, a haze, a gate, and places with names.

3
00:00:13,074 --> 00:00:16,117
I did not model any of it.

4
00:00:16,567 --> 00:00:20,480
I added about twenty lines to the same file.

5
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:28,202
Two of today's fields only show on flat walls, so the ruin needs one box.

6
00:00:28,652 --> 00:00:32,565
If you did last lecture's exercise you have it.

7
00:00:33,015 --> 00:00:35,189
If not, add it now.

8
00:00:35,639 --> 00:00:41,726
Six numbers: the middle, then half the width, half the height, half the length.

9
00:00:42,176 --> 00:00:44,785
And a passage to the Nave.

10
00:00:45,985 --> 00:00:51,637
This line goes on the ruin, and it names a look. Five words.

11
00:00:52,087 --> 00:00:56,435
Rock is asteroids, and it is what you had already.

12
00:00:56,885 --> 00:01:00,363
Plates are flat pieces laid over every wall.

13
00:01:00,813 --> 00:01:03,422
Blocks are the same with thickness.

14
00:01:03,872 --> 00:01:06,915
Ribs are plates with bars across them.

15
00:01:07,365 --> 00:01:09,974
None is no walls at all.

16
00:01:10,424 --> 00:01:21,728
The game builds a wall from a few hundred small pieces: about four hundred and fifty rocks for this ruin, or three hundred and seventy plates.

17
00:01:22,178 --> 00:01:23,917
I am keeping rock.

18
00:01:24,367 --> 00:01:26,541
This place is a cave.

19
00:01:27,741 --> 00:01:29,915
Say only where it changes.

20
00:01:30,365 --> 00:01:34,713
The Gallery was built later, so the Gallery gets blocks.

21
00:01:35,163 --> 00:01:39,946
Every room without a line of its own takes the ruin's.

22
00:01:40,396 --> 00:01:42,570
So do the tunnels, always.

23
00:01:43,020 --> 00:01:44,324
Now the Vault.

24
00:01:44,774 --> 00:01:46,948
Art names the piece itself.

25
00:01:47,398 --> 00:01:54,354
The game has six asteroid shapes, numbered six to eleven, and a rock wall mixes them.

26
00:01:54,804 --> 00:01:58,717
With this line the Vault is cut from one.

27
00:01:59,167 --> 00:02:00,907
Art picks the piece.

28
00:02:01,357 --> 00:02:03,096
Walls picks the look.

29
00:02:04,296 --> 00:02:06,904
Three dials, all on the ruin.

30
00:02:07,354 --> 00:02:09,963
Seed decides which rock goes where.

31
00:02:10,413 --> 00:02:19,109
The same number builds the same ruin every time, so your players and you are looking at the same place.

32
00:02:19,559 --> 00:02:23,472
Debris is the loose rock drifting inside the rooms.

33
00:02:23,922 --> 00:02:26,096
Sixty if you say nothing.

34
00:02:26,546 --> 00:02:27,850
I want thirty.

35
00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:32,648
Gaps is how much of a built wall is missing.

36
00:02:33,098 --> 00:02:37,880
It is a number from nought to one, not a percentage.

37
00:02:38,330 --> 00:02:41,809
Nought point two is one piece in five.

38
00:02:42,259 --> 00:02:47,041
It only touches flat walls, so here that is the Gallery.

39
00:02:47,491 --> 00:02:51,839
One is no wall at all, and so is two.

40
00:02:53,039 --> 00:02:55,648
One more line on the ruin.

41
00:02:56,098 --> 00:02:59,576
Atmosphere fills the whole place with one cloud.

42
00:03:00,026 --> 00:03:02,200
Seven colors, in small letters.

43
00:03:02,650 --> 00:03:06,998
Leave the line out, or write none, for no cloud.

44
00:03:08,198 --> 00:03:10,372
A new kind of record.

45
00:03:10,822 --> 00:03:14,300
Three hashes, and Relic: hollow, like a room.

46
00:03:14,750 --> 00:03:19,533
But this is a prop: a thing standing in the ruin.

47
00:03:19,983 --> 00:03:21,287
Prop is where.

48
00:03:21,737 --> 00:03:26,085
Fourteen hundred along is the middle of the first tunnel.

49
00:03:26,535 --> 00:03:35,665
Dress is what, and how big: a ring, four times its size, which makes it a little wider than the tunnel.

50
00:03:36,115 --> 00:03:40,028
Facing is which way it looks: at the Nave.

51
00:03:40,478 --> 00:03:42,652
A prop takes no space.

52
00:03:43,102 --> 00:03:44,841
You fly through it.

53
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:48,335
These plain shapes come with the game.

54
00:03:48,785 --> 00:03:54,437
Real gates and statues come in an art pack, in sets called kits.

55
00:03:54,887 --> 00:03:58,365
Your mission does not have the pack yet.

56
00:03:58,815 --> 00:04:05,337
But you can write a list, and the game takes the first word it knows.

57
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:07,961
Today that is the ring.

58
00:04:09,161 --> 00:04:11,770
Last kind of record: a point.

59
00:04:12,220 --> 00:04:13,524
A named spot.

60
00:04:13,974 --> 00:04:16,148
Three numbers, inside a room.

61
00:04:16,598 --> 00:04:20,076
And roles, which say what it is for.

62
00:04:20,526 --> 00:04:24,004
One role means something to the game: entrance.

63
00:04:24,454 --> 00:04:29,672
The name of the ruin on the map moves to this point.

64
00:04:30,122 --> 00:04:33,600
Any other role is a word of mine.

65
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:37,528
The Altar, in the middle of the Vault.

66
00:04:37,978 --> 00:04:47,109
The game stands an invisible marker there, and when a ship gets close it turns into a contact with this name.

67
00:04:47,559 --> 00:04:50,602
The Niche is the same, and hidden.

68
00:04:51,052 --> 00:04:55,835
Hidden is for a crew in suits, later in this class.

69
00:04:56,285 --> 00:04:58,893
For a ship it changes nothing.

70
00:05:00,093 --> 00:05:01,093
Lint. Clean.

71
00:05:01,543 --> 00:05:05,891
A misspelled style: it tells me, and lists the five.

72
00:05:06,341 --> 00:05:12,428
A point with two numbers: it tells me the place will not be made.

73
00:05:12,878 --> 00:05:15,922
Now the name of the ring. Clean.

74
00:05:16,372 --> 00:05:22,893
Lint does not check that word today, and the game would simply build no ring.

75
00:05:23,343 --> 00:05:28,126
So read your Dress and Art lines yourself, letter by letter.

76
00:05:29,326 --> 00:05:32,804
The name is at the way in now.

77
00:05:33,254 --> 00:05:34,559
Inside: the haze.

78
00:05:35,009 --> 00:05:38,922
The ring, across the tunnel. Through it. The Nave.

79
00:05:39,372 --> 00:05:46,328
Up to the Vault, and there: The Altar, on the map, because I am close enough.

80
00:05:46,778 --> 00:05:50,257
And the Gallery: built walls, with pieces missing.

81
00:05:51,457 --> 00:05:56,239
Change the Gallery to ribs and take more of it away.

82
00:05:56,689 --> 00:06:01,472
Put something on the altar: a point can be dressed too.

83
00:06:01,922 --> 00:06:04,965
Add a hidden place of your own.

84
00:06:05,415 --> 00:06:11,502
Then break one line where lint can see it and one where it cannot.

85
00:06:11,952 --> 00:06:16,300
Next time, a place says something when the crew arrives.
